~ start
Pikpik: …There you are. Finally. Took you long enough.
# He waddles out, still brushing dust off his wings.
Pikpik: So. While you were taking your extremely concerning nap, the whole city kind of… collapsed. Not a metaphor. I mean literally. Stuff fell. Sparks everywhere. People ran. I tried to find you. Found rubble instead. Thought you were pancake-shaped now. But you're not. So that's already the best part of today.
# You just stare at him, trying to grasp anything familiar.
Pikpik: Yeah. Thought so. I could tell by the 'please reboot me' look on your face.
# He hops forward, lowering his voice.
Pikpik: Listen. Something went wrong. Really wrong. The city doesn't collapse on its own. And everyone's memories gone, poof. You included. But I remember. I don't know why it's just me, but I do.
# He gestures at the destroyed landscape.
Pikpik: And we can fix this. Bit by bit. Place by place. But I can't do it alone. You've always been the one who helps put things back in order.
# He tilts his head.
Pikpik: So, you in? Because I found something weird nearby and I think it's connected.
=> END
=> END